(SECTION 5: LT POWER AND CONTROL CABLES) Tj T*
(i\) LT power cables shall be aluminium conductor, XLPE insulated, armoured, PVC sheathed, 1.1 kV) Tj T*
(grade, complying with IS 7098 \(Part 1\):1988.) Tj T*
(ii\) The size of the main feeder cable shall be 3.5 core 300 mm2.) Tj T*
(iii\) Maximum continuous conductor temperature of the cables shall be 90 ?. Copper conductor) Tj T*
(control cables of 2.5 mm2, PVC insulated, 1.1 kV grade shall comply with IS 1554 \(Part 1\).) Tj T*
(iv\) Class 2 stranded conductors complying with IS 8130 shall be used.) Tj T*
(v\) Cables shall be run in RCC trenches or on perforated trays as per drawings.) Tj T*
(vi\) Double compression glands and crimped lugs shall be used for all cable terminations.) Tj T*
(vii\) The maker's name, size, voltage grade and year of manufacture shall be marked on every) Tj T*
(drum.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 6: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(i\) Each assembly shall undergo routine verification as laid down in IS/IEC 61439-1. The bidder) Tj T*
(shall furnish type test certificates of the offered panel design issued by a NABL accredited) Tj T*
(laboratory.) Tj T*
(ii\) Testing of the cables shall be done as per IS 10810.) Tj T*
(iii\) Each consignment of cables shall be accompanied by routine test certificates.) Tj T*
(iv\) Before despatch, the Engineer-in-charge will inspect the equipment at the maker's works.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(i\) Detailed shop drawings are to be submitted by the contractor for approval not later than 21) Tj T*
(calendar days after the award of work. On completion the contractor shall hand over three) Tj T*
(copies of the O&M manuals.) Tj T*
(ii\) The contractor shall guarantee the whole installation for 12 months after handing over) Tj T*
(against faulty design, materials and workmanship.) Tj T*
(iii\) Operation and routine maintenance training shall be given by the contractor to the) Tj T*
